    "source": "08_parliamentary_review.txt",
    "text": "Parliamentary Review of Civic Services Reform\n\nThe parliamentary review of the Civic Services Reform Act began in 2024.\nSofia Bennett presented evidence from regional councils.\nDaniel Reed presented findings from the implementation review committee.\n\nThe review concluded that regional digital service grants had improved access to several public services.\nIt recommended continuing the grant program with stronger auditing requirements.\n\nElena Marlow welcomed the review and called for greater transparency in grant reporting.\nMarcus Hale supported the auditing recommendation.\nPriya Sen submitted evidence about the Riverland Regional Council's experience.\n\nThe recommendations were sent to the parliamentary committee for consideration.",
