    "source": "06_civic_services_act.txt",
    "text": "Civic Services Reform Act\n\nThe Civic Services Reform Act was drafted after negotiations between the Federal Reform Coalition and the National Development Party.\nElena Marlow advocated stronger transparency requirements.\nMarcus Hale proposed additional regional infrastructure funding.\nSofia Bennett coordinated the final parliamentary amendments.\n\nThe act was passed in 2022.\nIts implementation framework created regional digital service grants.\nLocal councils could apply for grants to modernize public-service systems.\n\nDaniel Reed later joined the implementation review committee.\nThe committee published its first progress report in 2023.",
