    "source": "05_national_development_party.txt",
    "text": "National Development Party\n\nThe National Development Party was led by Marcus Hale from 2019 to 2023.\nMarcus Hale appointed Sofia Bennett as parliamentary affairs coordinator.\nSofia Bennett coordinated discussions with the Federal Reform Coalition.\n\nThe National Development Party supported the Civic Services Reform Act after several amendments.\nThe party proposed additional funding for regional infrastructure.\nMarcus Hale presented the amended proposal during a parliamentary session in 2022.\n\nAfter the 2022 election, Sofia Bennett became minister for regional administration.\nShe continued work on the Civic Services Reform Act and its implementation framework.",
