    "source": "04_federal_reform.txt",
    "text": "Federal Reform Coalition\n\nThe Federal Reform Coalition was formed in 2018 by Elena Marlow and Daniel Reed.\nElena Marlow became the coalition's first chairperson.\nDaniel Reed served as policy director.\n\nThe coalition proposed the Civic Services Reform Act in 2020.\nThe proposal focused on digital public services, government transparency, and local administrative funding.\nIn 2021, the coalition joined negotiations with the National Development Party.\n\nElena Marlow supported a parliamentary committee to review the reform proposal.\nDaniel Reed prepared the coalition's policy brief for the committee.\nThe coalition later worked with regional councils to revise its funding provisions.",
